# What Docker may send to the builder. The build copies only package.json,
# the lockfile, tsconfig.json, src, tools, bin, schema and n8n, but Docker sends
# the whole context first, so anything not excluded here reaches the builder
# even though it never reaches the image. Credentials and people data must
# never be in that set.

# Credentials and configuration with real values
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
jml.config.yaml
jml.config.*.yaml
!jml.config.example.yaml
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
service-account*.json
credentials.json
tools/lint/denylist.local.txt

# People data, state and the audit log
data/
audit/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Nothing the build needs
.git/
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
test/
docs/
.github/
*.md
!n8n/README.md
